uutils/awk at the pinned commit does not compile for Windows: `parser/src/lib.rs` imports `PathBuf`
twice under `#[cfg(not(unix))]` (E0252), because the unconditional import just below already brings it
in. `Cow`, the other name in that import, is used only inside `#[cfg(not(unix))] fn make_path`, so the
cfg'd import keeps `Cow` and drops the duplicate `PathBuf`. Drop this patch when upstream fixes it.

diff --git a/parser/src/lib.rs b/parser/src/lib.rs
index f96debf..876e8a7 100644
--- a/parser/src/lib.rs
+++ b/parser/src/lib.rs
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ mod sexpr;
 mod tests;
 
 #[cfg(not(unix))]
-use std::{borrow::Cow, path::PathBuf};
+use std::borrow::Cow;
 use std::{
     fs::File,
     mem::{replace, take},
